Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML card that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only CSS (no JavaScript) and works in modern browsers.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container to center the card */
body {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #f0f0f0;
}

/* Card wrapper – gives perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* Creates depth */
}

/* The actual card – positioned relative so we can transform it */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D children */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate around Y axis */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card-face {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: white;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b); /* Warm gradient */
}

/* Back face styling – rotated 180° so it shows after flip */
.card-back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6a11cb, #2575fc); /* Cool gradient */
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="card-face card-front">
            <div>Front Side</div>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="card-face card-back">
            <div>Back Side</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a `perspective` so the 3D rotation has depth. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces and gets the `transform` applied on hover. |
| `.card-face` | Common styles for front/back faces. |
| `.card-front` / `.card-back` | Each face has its own background. The back face is pre‑rotated 180° so it becomes visible after the card flips. |

Feel free to replace the gradients or add images/text inside the `<div>` tags to suit your design. Enjoy!
